# Image & Screenshot Rules

## Folder Structure

```
images/
  {NN}-{kebab-case-article-title}/
    descriptive-name.png
```

- `NN` = article number (matches the article file)
- Folder name = article number + kebab-case title
- Example: `images/36-settlement-and-nft-transfer/settlement-activity.png`

## Naming Conventions

| Type | Format | Example |
|------|--------|---------|
| Dashboard | `{role}-{section}-dashboard.png` | `issuer-asset-sale-dashboard.png` |
| Form/Modal | `{action}-{context}.png` | `create-deal-wizard-step1.png` |
| Detail Page | `{entity}-details.png` | `deal-details-page.png` |
| Status/Lifecycle | `{entity}-lifecycle-stepper.png` | `deal-lifecycle-stepper.png` |
| Table/List | `{entity}-list.png` | `pool-list-issuer.png` |
| Icon/SVG | `{feature}-icon.svg` | `asset-sale-icon.svg` |

## Format Rules

- **Screenshots:** PNG format, CSS scale (not device scale)
- **Icons/Diagrams:** SVG format when possible
- **Full viewport:** Screenshots should capture the full relevant area
- **No personal data:** Blur or use test accounts only
- **Consistent sizing:** Use the same browser width for all captures

## Capturing Screenshots

### Using Playwright MCP
```
1. browser_navigate → target URL
2. browser_wait_for → key element visible
3. browser_take_screenshot → { scale: "css", filename: "path.png" }
```

