## Referencing Images in Articles

```markdown
![Issuer Asset Sale Dashboard](images/32-asset-sale-overview/issuer-asset-sale-dashboard.png)
```

- Always use relative paths from the article file
- Always provide meaningful alt text (not just "screenshot")
- Place images AFTER the paragraph they illustrate
- One image per concept — don't stack multiple images without text between them

## Which Articles Need Screenshots

| Document Type | Screenshot Expectation |
|---------------|----------------------|
| C (Navigation) | REQUIRED — show the actual UI being described |
| D (How-To) | REQUIRED — show each major step |
| J (Overview) | RECOMMENDED — show the module dashboard |
| K (Workflow) | RECOMMENDED — show key workflow stages |
| L (Review) | RECOMMENDED — show the review interface |
| A, E, F, G, H, I | OPTIONAL — conceptual articles may not need them |
| B | OPTIONAL — role descriptions rarely need screenshots |
